  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development would result in the loss of a family sized unit, thereby failing to comply with policy H11.1 of Merton Local Plan 2024 ",
    "The application fails to provide sufficient information to demonstrate that future occupiers would be provided with an acceptable standard of residential accommodation. In particular, insufficient information has been submitted regarding the provision, size, layout and functionality of external amenity space, and no fully furnished floor plans have been provided to demonstrate that the proposed accommodation would be functional and fit for purpose. The proposal has therefore failed to demonstrate that it would provide a high-quality living environment for future occupiers, contrary Policies D4 and D6 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies D12.1 and D12.3 of the Merton Local Plan 2024.",
    "In the absence of satisfactory and convenient access to cycle storage facilities, the scheme is contrary to policy T16.2 of&nbsp; Merton’s Local Plan 2024 and T5 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "In the absence of adequate refuse and recycling storage facilities for the development, the applicant has not demonstrated that the scheme would not adversely impact on the free flow of traffic in the locality to the detriment of highway and pedestrian safety and result in material harm to the visual amenity&nbsp; of the area.&nbsp; The scheme is contrary to, in particular, Policies D4, SI 7 &amp; SI 8 of the London Plan 2021,&nbsp; Merton Local Plan 2024 policy D12.2, D12.3 and W14.4.",
    "The application has failed to demonstrate that the development would be air quality neutral. No Air Quality Neutral Statement has been submitted and, consequently, the Local Planning Authority is unable to adequately assess the air quality impacts of the proposal or determine whether it would comply with the Borough&#39;s air quality objectives. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy SI1 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy P15.10 of the Merton Local Plan 2024.",
    "In the absence of a fire safety strategy, the applicant has failed to demonstrate that the development would provide the highest standard of fire safety, thereby failing to comply with policy D12 of the London Plan 2021."
  ],
